{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1515137405,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODYyMTE2ODk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2059","origin":"github"},"title":"Support GigaDB as a data provider","message":"GigaDB (http://gigadb.org) is a large database of public domain data across a variety of topics. They use datacite for metadata (i.e. datacite can be queried for their metadata), each dataset has a DOI, there is no required authentication, data access is via plain FTP.\n\nDemo dataset, randomly picked from fontpage:\n\nhttp://gigadb.org/dataset/100397\n\nFTP site:\n\nftp://penguin.genomics.cn/pub/10.5524/100001_101000/100397/\n\nIt looks as if all datasets are stored under this common URL:\n\nftp://penguin.genomics.cn/pub/10.5524/\n\nThe final part of a full URL comes from the respective DOI, not yet sure what the second to last part is. However, only four unique values exist for that.","files":null}]}